We discovered that GitHub Actions was generating different signing certificates on different builds.

As a result:

- SHA-1 changed between builds.
- SHA-256 could also change.
- Google Sign-In stopped working when the new fingerprint was not registered.
- Android refused to update the previously installed APK.
- The user had to uninstall and reinstall the application.

This must be permanently fixed.

